{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games","id":1516202,"title":"What do vampires know of other clans, in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T05:41:37-07:00","id":1516202,"title":"What do vampires know of other clans, in your games?","content":"Sometimes it feels like characters have access to the clanbooks, especially when you read the clan stereotypes sidebar, although I feel like they probably shouldn't. How about you guys? <hr /><br /> I think I might borrow MtA's Lore ability to represent a pc's knowledge of other clans*, honestly. You'll like learn over time the basic structure and goals of a clan in order to deal with them, and some vampires make a point to be scholars of their kind, or are ex-converts, and Elders are more worldly, but intimate knowledge of other clan cultures is not <i>that</i> widespread; you generally know what that particular clan wants the world to know about them, no more.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I would make the first dot free, honestly.<br /> So, WIP but with every clan being measured on their own, maybe like:<br /> <br /> \u2022You know they exist, what they do, and some other basic knowledge and rumours<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">[The Tremere are disliked, have a strict hierarchal structure called the Pyramid in groups called Chantries run by a guy called the Regent; Lasombra are social darwinists who manipulate shadows and have a connection to the Church, there seems to be bad blood with the Ventrue]</span><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 You know the basics of their history and some legends, some basic grasp of their structure.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">[You can name their clan founder, their important players, their historical activities (exactly why the Tremere are hated, and by who, and stuff like the usurping of Saulot and Cappadocius, for example). You know that the warrior caste is only one branch of the Assamites. You know what the Gerousia is, and the difference between a Tremere Lord and a Regent.]</span><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Structures fully understood<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">[The Assamites have three castes and a split between the Web of Knives and everyone else; you know the role of the Ephorate and other structures in Clan Ventrue]</span><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Finer distinctions understood<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">[The Setites are a mytery cult and all their faces are just avenues deeper in; Clan Giovanni actually consists of something like 12 families, of various importance; Each rank in the Pyramid is divided into seven &quot;circles of mystery&quot;, and the clan has secret societies]</span><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 You know so much about this clan you may as well be a member, and probably not the stuff they like you knowing. Or maybe you're just a very dedicated convert to the service of Sutekh or Haqim, or something.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">[You know about Vienna's worm problem; The Giovanni pursue world domination via the Endless Night; the Ventrue are worried about the Daeva; the Nosferatu are being hunted by a sibling bloodline called the Nictuku]</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> If you're running on basic knowledge in the Cam, six of the core seven are familiar enough*, with the Tremere being a little more secretive but not a total unknown. They have a &quot;pyramid&quot;, they're wizards, they're useful but don't trust 'em. The two Sabbat clans are alien monsters leading some kind of apocalypse cult; Lasombra are goths with a fetish for catholic iconography who can control shadows; this doesn't sound scary, but everyone who's ever seen obtenebration in action gets this far away look in their eyes that suggests you should probably avoid them. Tzimisce are... face stealing shape-changers or demons or something with a hobby for making human furniture? (Which might be because of an alien disease?)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Though some deeper lore, like the Ventrue's paranoia about the &quot;secret masters&quot; and the Nosferatu vs Nictuku, are much better guarded secrets.</span>\u200b<br /> <br /> In the Sabbat core six are still familiar**, as are the Lasombra and Tzimisce, but the Tremere are the Usurpers; mysterious, occluded boogeymen who will kidnap you and do terrible things (which are terrible things that aren't ok, unlike the stuff everybody else does, because they're not Cainites; they're creepy wizards who basically stole vampires' faces to wear as a Halloween mask, or something).<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">**Although if you got a neonate from the Sabbat and the Cam to compare notes on the Ventrue as they know them, they'd probably get a bit confused.</span><br /> <br /> The Independents are mysteries that you may not hear about until you're decades into your unlife and won't truly understand unless you join them.<br /> The Assamites are a group of hitmen, rumour suggests they're cannibals and religious fanatics (whether this religion is a weird vampire blood cult or a shallow stereotype of Islam depends on who you ask).<br /> The Setites are... New Age cultists with a thing for snakes? Fixers? Pimps? Drug dealers? Self-help gurus? Antique dealers? MLMs? Who knows! They're very friendly though...<br /> The Giovanni are as that old Toreador stereotype says of them; they're charming, and pleasant to do business with, but unsettling for reasons you can't put your finger on. You know they're &quot;necromancers&quot; (ghosts are real?) and there's unsubstantiated rumours about mafia and... <i>weird </i>fetishes.<br /> The Ravnos are compulsive liars are inherently prone to criminality, what more could you possibly need to know? <span style=\"font-size:11px\">(...what the hell are you talking about? &quot;They have a clan culture&quot;? What are you going on about demons for? Fairies!? Fairies don't exist, what are you five? Grow up!)</span><br /> <br /> And for anything else; &quot;what's a bloodline?&quot;\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-26-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T06:59:00-07:00","id":1516206,"title":"","content":"This is how I see it:<br /> It is quite simple:<br /> <b>Knowledge is power</b><br /> <br /> Sun Tzu said Know the enemy and know yourself in a hundred battles you will never be in peril. When you are ignorant of the enemy but know yourself, your chances of winning or losing are equal. If ignorant both of your enemy and of yourself, you are certain in every battle to be in peril.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, with all the byzantine politics and machiavellian schemes, Cainites are suprisingly... honest and reliable, dare Is say, trustworthy.<br /> The Vampire society is basically built around &quot;<i>Boons</i>&quot;.<br /> Favors are the currency of the undead and agreeing to do or owe a favor is a big deal among vampires.<br /> And thats requires <i>trust</i> the other party will keep it word, and that trust is soemwhat earned but very easy to lost - and once you lost it? You are dead in the Vampire society<br /> No one make deals with a know liar - simply not wort to risk an eternity of horrible reputation and be an outcast socially\u200b<br /> No matter the time period, the clan, the bloodline, awesome powers at the end of the day (night?) all you have is your reputation<br /> sure you have can move to another Domain, but if you are not preapred to build a totally new persona, an alternate idenity with a clean slate, you are toast - and even then you have to watch over your back to make sure no one uncover your dirty little secret<br /> <br /> And thats bring us to another crucial point:<br /> Vampires are vain and proud creatures - they are cats basically<br /> A vampire is porud, he is the member of a given Clan and his ancestors, and almost every Domain, it is part of the intorduciton to list your ancestors, starting with your Clan and with your Sire at leats to the third degree, better yet, back to Caine himself! <br /> Reputation and Pride <br /> These two tings are the grease that make possible to the Vampire Society to &quot;work&quot;<br /> Especially when the Nosferatu are around ready to provide a backgroudn check...<br /> Actually even without the reputation and pride thing, the Nosferatu would be enough to spread the word, sell the information about the potential enemies of the Domain... <br /> The three combined and paired with the favorite past time of vampires, gossiping? <br /> Any self respecting Vampire (especially if tutored by her Sire - and remember you can't afford a &quot;faliure&quot; Child, your Child have to be prepared so she wont be a source of shame - sure, accidents happens, but it is in your best intrest to teach you Child to not only know the basics and stereotypes, but possible have a head start - Vampires are really like partents who have childrends only to make themselves improtant in the eyes of the other parents. Everything boils down to human nature and every vampire was a Huma nat one point) will learn as much as possible form any source to preapre, to survive! To earn her freedom, when her Sire finally nods, okay, you are ready to move as far away as possible and carry my legacy... but remember I will watching you. And your Child and so on... so a good advice: Don't fuck up and be a source of shame<br /> <br /> Sure, deeper knowledge requires Lore background, but first and foremost Vampires are while Predators who hates anyone on their territory... they are social. They need other vampires, the community, the system, everything that is echoes the Human needs: either to be on top, either to have soemone to tell you what to do or either to be the part something and be among your kind <br /> Vampire need other vampires to have them around so they could show them how better they are then the rest<br /> As I said Reputation and Pride <br /> Sure, in your first nights you can afford (or not, depending of.. several factors) to be a &quot;dumb Child&quot; and embarrass yourself on the streets, or even among friends and your coterie (we all been there, as humans... society is cruel, embarrass yourself and especially in this modern age with all the gadgets and such, even your great grandchild will hear about how you accidently in a hurry picked up your mothers underpants and only in the lockerrom noticed when all the other guys laughed)...<br /> But in an Elysium? Not that much<br /> Those polite nods and faint smiles will haunt you forever after you said &quot;oh Assamites? That group of hitmen of alegedly cannibals and religious fanatics?&quot; <br /> Not really would fly - Herpies will tear you apart figuretively. Then your Sire, literally. <br /> So if you want to survive your first year, the first thing you should do to grab a Nosferatu and without using the word &quot;rat&quot; or &quot;sewer&quot; ask him what it would cost you to know everything you need to know an your Sire might forgot to mention. Of course leving oout the Sire part...<br /> <br /> Now other inhabitants of the Night is more tricky<br /> Ghost are known, after all, vampires had a literal Clan of Death and now the famous/infamous Necromancers but geting info about them require some legwork<br /> Werewolves are just Lupines - but this depends on several factor (and the Game) you need a Weerwolf expert to know they are Garou and have Tribes and they don't need the full moon and so on - not much to talk about them, beasts of the are outside your territory, the City<br /> Fae... they are an extreme case, depending of the local Malkavians and if you have a Kyasid bartender in the Elysium <br /> Demons and all the other... well... depending really; either you were warned, kill every Baali on sight, or heard about Lucifer grand entrerance above Los Angeles in live TV...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T07:38:09-07:00","id":1516212,"title":"","content":"I may have been focusing on the neonate perspective. As you grow older you will learn. Elders are, as I said, more worldly; enough to have a grasp of clan structures and what they value in order to deal with them... though I still don't want them knowing anything <i>too</i> substantial about each other. <br /> <br /> ... and the Children of Haqim <i>do</i> have a culture of cannibalism and religious fanaticism, so the fledgling isn't wrong.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't have that perspective discouraged, per se. I like having the non-Camarilla clans be used as an example to the Ivory Tower's young about how <i>not</i> to live your unlife. Look how much better we are; how good you have it. Monsters, weirdos and wackjob cultists the lot of them. Oh, don't be <i>stupid</i> enough to say that to their face, but we're all thinking it... <span style=\"font-size:11px\">and pay no attention to your great-grandsire's little ancestor cult and plans to build a Gehenna bunker that he's hidden behind that door. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T09:10:57-07:00","id":1516217,"title":"","content":"Since we play ancilla in our game. Our characters have somewhat more knowledge on how the other clans work and know that they are more varied then at first glance, But my Brujah &amp; Malkavian certainly don't know all the details about what caused the formation of the Hecate and just think it's a quasi sect that all varied death clans joined but not much more then that. <br /> <br /> So in your game terms is that my Brujah would max out at 2 dots at best and my Malkavian would rank a 3 the most as he loves mysteries and puzzles and is more outgoing of the two kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-26-2023, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T14:06:42-07:00","id":1516252,"title":"","content":"It tends to vary depending on context. For example a 5 year carmarilla neonate will have a pretty good grasp on the sects clans if they interact with them but it gets more hazy out of sect.<br /> <br /> An in game example I recall was a brujah neonate during a siege knew lasombra had a obtenerbration and the tzmisce had visccitude and a basic understanding of what they're genrally like. But didn't know the other clan disciplines they possessed. By contrast he had a very good understanding of the ventrue and tremere were like to the point the gm said it was fair he could guesstimate that the tremere and nosferatu would pay for tzmisce grimoires on the Occult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-27-2023, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T16:15:29-07:00","id":1516275,"title":"","content":"I guess just the basic, something like that:<br /> <br /> Brujah: Anarchs, idealistic and impulsive, prone to anger, cannon fodder in most cases, but have some unity among themselves and some of them are capable leaders, but this is very rare. Use them, but beware of them.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Similar to Brujah but without the idealistic part, wild as animals and don't feel good in cities, but aren't necessarily dumb, if you see one of them that looks more animal than human then stay away from him.<br /> <br /> Toreador: Pretty face, snub nose, dresses well, thinks they knows more than they actually does, some say they can still fuck, are good with gossip, but don't trust them.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Monsters that live in the sewers, they know a lot of things even what you think they don't know, they usually open their mouths when they receive the right payment along with some praise, but they can still screw you by giving you the wrong information, don't provoke them and avoid them if you can.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: Same as the toreador, but with more money and more bosses, as dangerous as their money.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Mages and usurpers, that says all you need to know and why you shouldn't trust them, associating with them has its advantages, but be aware of the risks. (Script tool)<br /> <br /> Malkavian: Unpredictable freaks and bores until proven otherwise, which usually isn't the case, avoid destroying them, even if it's very tempting.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Think of a Ventrue who dresses like a Toreador and uses shadows.<br /> <br /> Tzimice: ???<br /> <br /> Ravnos: Arms merchants and mercenaries, do not trust them under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> Ministry: Treacherous snakes, if you can, rip off the head and don't listen to anything they tell you.<br /> <br /> Giovanni: Mafiosi and dangerous, don't underestimate them and remember where there is one there must be more. Try not to provoke them and don't even go near their relatives.<br /> <br /> Saulot: Two options: Avoid them, they always bring problems; What is a Saulot?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T22:30:54-07:00","id":1516315,"title":"","content":"Camarilla Kindred are more likely to know about how Sabbat Clans operate, if there's been a crusade on their city within their unlifetime, or not too long before. (Which could mean anything from a few years to a few centuries). An Elder or Ancillae, if they're in a chatty mood, might have shared some &quot;war stories&quot; about Tzimisce flesh abominations during a siege, or the shadows coiling out from a manhole cover and dragging a ghoul into the sewer.<br /> <br /> Of course, even in a Sabbat crusade, the &quot;rank and file&quot; Sabbat fighters are likely to be shovelheads and young packs. Often from the Antitribu, as many Lasombra and Tzimisce consider it beneath them to stand at the front lines. Not unless there's a great deal of glory to be won, anyway. If Camarilla vampires encounter any Magistrates or Fiends, it'll be young licks just coming into their powers.<br /> <br /> Antitribu can be illustrative, though, in the more martial applications of even &quot;familiar&quot; Disciplines. Camarilla society tends to disincentivize starting fights at the best of times. So Neonates may be ignorant of what Discipline powers can do at higher levels, or how they can be applied to violence or as asymmetrical war tactics. (A random mortal doesn't need to know the briefcase they've been Dominated to deliver to Elysium is actually full of plastic explosives. So their impromptu s*icide bombing technically doesn't violate the rules of the Discipline.)<br /> <br /> This can apply to both Disciplines outside a PC's Clan, and even powers within it. The Gangrel PC may not be aware they can eventually possess the body of an animal. Especially if their sire wasn't around to instruct them. If their formative nights involved tangling with Sabbat Gangrel or Nosferatu, though, they might have a better idea about it. Let alone what <i>Elders</i> could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T01:59:25-07:00","id":1516326,"title":"","content":"Depends on your city, your sire, how talkative people are at elysium etc,<br /> <br /> ...and how many dots you put into knowledges... <br /> <br /> Many well intentioned sires will provide plentiful information (some of which might be wrong) while others will get nothing or even disinformation, generally in cases where the neonate is disposable or the sire is desperate and wants to dangle carrots in front of the neonate so they can do work for them immediately.. <br /> <br /> Some places are just remote and there might not even be a second bloodline there, while others have representatives from every major bloodline and more with a sizeable scholar club ensuring good information. <br /> <br /> Some clans, like the Ventrue, are proud of themselves and are really important to other clans and keep relatively good records so it's very easy to learn about them and their and local history. The Lasombra, in contrast, you're probably just going to learn about how they're massive bastards and the best ways to avoid them. If we're talking Samedi... It's all hearsay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T05:14:36-07:00","id":1516330,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to contribute but I do have a couple of thoughts from a meta perspective.<br /> <br /> Firstly a lot of it is down to your players, if you have players who haven't read all the books and don't know all the lore then it's easier to surprise them with something. Whereas with experienced players it's down to wether or not they're capable of playing 'ignorant' characters. Good players with lots of canon knowledge can be easy to work with but players who utilise their player knowledge for an in-game edge for their character are a pain to deal with.<br /> <br /> Secondly, when adding Lore skills, remember that forcing players to put points into them is restricting their builds, but giving them free Lore ratings based on their character's knowledge/background/etc enables them to RP with that Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:51:41-07:00","id":1516392,"title":"","content":"Vampires are, in fact, incredibly ignorant in my games.<br /> <br /> Most Neonates over a year old know the following:<br /> <br /> * You can probably deduce how vampires are made from context.<br /> * Sunlight and fire are instinctual. No one needs to be taught this anymore than blood is yummy.<br /> * There's the Clans of the Camarilla (Brujah, Malk, Nosferatu, Ventrue, Toreador, Gangrel, and Tremere--maybe Assamite and Lasombra depending on the year)<br /> * They're generally aware of Caitiff and Thin Bloods these days. Neonates generally get taught to treat them like trash if they're not either themselves.<br /> * They're aware Lupines exist, some are skeptical. It's a &quot;friend of a friend&quot; sort of thing unless you live in Chicago or Milwaukee or Vancouver.<br /> * They're aware Blood Magic exists but not magic in general (the only wizards you know exist are Tremere)<br /> * There's Princes, Primogen, and Sheriff<br /> * <b>They all know the Masquerade</b><br /> * There are rules to vampire existence. You probably have to ask about them other than the Masquerade. Less the &quot;Laws of the Camarilla&quot; and more, &quot;Don't make any more vampires without permission.&quot;, &quot;Elders get pissy if you feed in their turf.&quot;, and &quot;Introduce yourself to the boss vampire in an area if you enter a new area. Don't worry, they'll find you.&quot;<br /> * There's a big vampire Illuminati called the Camarilla but no one deals with it beyond the Prince and Sheriff level generally<br /> * There's a vampire resistance that amounts more to street gangs and constant complaining called the Anarchs.<br /> * Older People (like, over 10 years) sometimes mention the Sabbat and clam up<br /> * There's other vampire Clans out there but you'll almost never meet them<br /> * Everyone will have heard the &quot;Caine origin&quot; but almost no one takes it seriously in the Modern Nights and it's more like a one sentence, &quot;Yeah, a lot of Older Vampires say Caine from the Bible was the first vampire. Sounds like a joke but there it is.&quot;<br /> * No one will have heard of the Antediluvians unless they're Tremere, Assamite, or Lasombra. Maybe Ventrue just to explain what &quot;Generation&quot; is.<br /> * Gehenna will NOT be spoken of<br /> * Ghouls are around constantly but unless you ask, no one will explain the Masquerade exception and generally it's like, &quot;Yeah, they're slaves. They drink blood and are addicts. Its fucked up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anything else requires an Occult score","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-27-2023, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T23:51:42-07:00","id":1516414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516392#post1516392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are, in fact, incredibly ignorant in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you consider how much info you could dump in a single hour, and that half the vampires are going to be charismatic types love the sound of their own voice/love gossip/want to appear supremely knowledgeable,. I find it unlikely that the average neonate would know so little. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T01:24:05-07:00","id":1516415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games#post1516202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes it feels like characters have access to the clanbooks, especially when you read the clan stereotypes sidebar, although I feel like they probably shouldn't. How about you guys? <hr /><br /> I think I might borrow MtA's Lore ability to represent a pc's knowledge of other clans*, honestly. You'll like learn over time the basic structure and goals of a clan in order to deal with them, and some vampires make a point to be scholars of their kind, or are ex-converts, and Elders are more worldly, but intimate knowledge of other clan cultures is not <i>that</i> widespread; you generally know what that particular clan wants the world to know about them, no more.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I consider that Lore or Knowledge or Involvement in regard to other Vampires Clans - or organizations, groups, and guilds of various Kindred - should be separated into<br /> <br /> 1) Practiical and on-the-ground ( or related to current events rigth on the streets ) fact confirmations, contribution, and invovelement.<br /> <br /> 2) Knowledge of legends, mysteries, special abiltiies, thinking ( and concepts, ideas, and emotions ) tendencies, and also confirmations about initiations and also knowledge in regard to usual and standard goals and ambitions. All in all, this would be both standard and higher supernatural ( and mystical and otherworldy ) knowledge, mysteries, and facts.<br /> <br /> 3) Knowldge about Clan ( and Company, Team, or Guild ) structures, predispositions of mundane gains and wealth, and also possibly social networks and diplomatic events and relations.<br /> <br /> <br /> This would be especially appropriate for protagonists and characters who would be particularly invested, caring, and involved about facts, confirmations, storytelling, lore, and legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T01:53:51-07:00","id":1516419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516392#post1516392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are, in fact, incredibly ignorant in my games.<br /> <br /> * No one will have heard of the Antediluvians unless they're Tremere, Assamite, or Lasombra. Maybe Ventrue just to explain what &quot;Generation&quot; is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anything else requires an Occult score</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, your game, so no one in the position to argue with you, I just would like to add, in my opinion the Camarilla Clans, as much as they are famous of denying the Antediluvian's existence, are strangely enough, - or not that strangely - are not different than then sabbat about them regarding existence<br /> Venture - no question tehere, they are expected to know their line back to Caine<br /> Toreador - they are either proud of Arikel alegedly the oldest Antediluvian and rub it under the nose of the Ventrue to piss of the &quot;Firstborns&quot; and familiar with the tale of the love between Absimilaird and Arikel, or don't really care.<br /> Malkavian - Okay, they are wyldcards, but considering the Madness Network and the constant whispering, voices of others or dead, alive yet to be Embraced Malkavians...? But okay, thay are the one that probably know nothing - yet spontaneusly burst of ancient tales and knowledge then blinking, what just happened?<br /> Nosferatu - their whole deal and Clan is centered around Absimiliard and the Nictuku tries to hunt them down... and the little stunt Baba Yaga pulled left a lasting impression on the world<br /> Brujah - no matter its age, I think you can't find a Brujah who don't know about Carthage and not blame the Venture for its fall...<br /> Tremere - as you said, know<br /> Gangrel - now this is a tricky one. Embraced and left alone to prove themselves... BUT after they managed to survive? The vital part of a Gangrel Gathering to tell stories and remember lineages up to Ennoia herself<br /> Lasombra - yep, they know and proud of it, either because they killed it, or either becasue they were better than their ancient and survived<br /> Tzimsice - See Lasombra<br /> Cappadocian/Hekata - yeah... you won't find one who don't know papa Cappadocius (or if you are a giovanni uncle Augie)<br /> Salubri - same as Cappadocian<br /> Ravnos - If the Week of Nightamre happened... ouch. If not, really depends of the region, the eastern Ravons are different than the western Ravnos who probably don&quot;t even know the Eastern Ravnos exist<br /> Followers of Set/Minisitry - another clan centered around their God, even the Ministry branch tho' becasue of the natrue of the Clan, varibaly degree of Truth<br /> Banu Haqim - Same as above with an added Ur-Shulgi\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-28-2023, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T02:13:47-07:00","id":1516420,"title":"","content":"Even vampires who love to hear themselves talk are more likely to talk about things unrelated to the state of the Jyhad, like their exploits in the Napoleonic wars or something.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is a setting of copious competing and concentric conspiracies. Where your baseline survival, both individually and as a faction, depend on keeping everything about you and how your kind operate as secret as possible. (Doubly so for Vampires, for whom being exposed means likely extinction). It behooves everyone within one or more of these conspiracies to keep their cards close to their chests. Both as a self-preservation matter, and because this same principle means the knowledge you carry can demand a high price.<br /> <br /> Knowledge - <i>actionable</i> knowledge - is a precious commodity and bargaining chip. You don't give that away for free. Your Elders teach you because they feel they need to (a truly ignorant Fledgling will shatter the Masquerade a million different ways by accident). Or because they have something to gain by you knowing something. Whether what they tell you is accurate, and whether your Elder knows it, is another matter entirely.<br /> <br /> A new Kindred (whether newly created or newly arrived) - unknown and unvetted - is a potential security risk. They could be a spy, future turncoat, or simply incompetent to the point of being dangerous. You don't tell them more than is needed, to minimize risks. They are told where to present themselves, and are told to fuck off when and if they stray too close to a more powerful vampire's territory. Established Elders, despite having all the time in the world, have no time to be giving the run-down about city politics to every fresh face. They have better things to do. Their underlings give out messages, and even THEY have better things to do than waste time coddling Neonates.<br /> <br /> Most new Kindred in town won't make it to the end of the century anyway. Unless they make themselves problems or assets, it's not worth devoting attention to them until they're at least Ancillae. When they have ostensibly proven their ability to survive and play the game.\u200b<br /> <br /> When a Neonate shows themselves as an asset, that still makes them a potential danger. Those with enough guile, social skills, and influence to force Elders to pay attention are the very kind of ambitious go-getters that try to climb the hierarchy of vampiric power. So even though there's much to gain from handing out knowledge, it's still a risk. The young whelps could use your kind instruction against you.<br /> <br /> Better to keep plenty of information back. Make the upstarts pay for every morsel of understanding they can get out of you. Bind them with webs of Debt and reliance on their betters. Make them play the Jyhad &quot;the right way&quot;. Until they've been &quot;properly&quot; incorporated into the existing power structures (hopefully a restructured one that, with the whelp's diligent efforts, improves YOUR position).<br /> <br /> A knowledgeable Neonate is one that's harder to control. They get ideas. If they know about other Clans, Bloodlines, and Sects, they can try to make alliances with them and not you. If they understand how the status quo functions - the forces that underpin it, and where it's weakest - they can disrupt it. They're the gutter trash. Unlike you, they have nothing to lose, and everything to gain.<br /> <br /> And if they learn enough, they may realize how little you actually know. They may realize you're not as privy to the secrets of the Jyhad as you pretend. Which is both dangerous, and deeply disturbing to be reminded of.<br /> <br /> No. It's better to keep those cards close. You have all eternity to take the whelp's measure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:08:39-07:00","id":1516422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516414#post1516414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you consider how much info you could dump in a single hour, and that half the vampires are going to be charismatic types love the sound of their own voice/love gossip/want to appear supremely knowledgeable,. I find it unlikely that the average neonate would know so little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Secrets are power among vampires and the majority of undead actually prefer to bargain for their information. As such, it's hard to know what's going on in another city let alone in ancient annals of Kindred history.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that the two Clans actually prone to showing information are the Nosferatu and Tremere who keep it all in-clan.<br /> <br /> The Brujah used to teach everyone but they've lost their reputation as the Learned Clan.<br /> <br /> Mind you, this isn't entirely by design. The Modern Nights have been something of a disaster in my games with how the Kindred race has evolved. A lot more vampires are created by accident, as a tool of war, or as disposable pawns only to get their freedom due to the Jhyad when their masters never intended them to be anything more than a tool under their iron fist in a velvet glove.<br /> <br /> But the ignorance of the Jyhad has an out of game purpose as well. It encourages PCs to know exactly what they're getting out of an Occult score.\u200b Those who put the EXP or Skill Points into it are showing that they are willing to make the effort to learn what the books have. The person who loves to talk more than most vampire NPCs as MyLifeIsScary describes is the PCs themselves. They can share all their own knowledge in-game once they make the effort to acquire it.<br /> <br /> It also provides an air of mystery to the setting that discovering secrets is important. The &quot;common knowledge&quot; of the books is incredibly valuable and it helps show why so many Elders are disdainful of your typical Lick who doesn't even know what a Salubri is.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> AKA what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> said.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-28-2023, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:11:07-07:00","id":1516423,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to see the different rationales, there are good points for whether more or less knowledge is sensible. One thing I notice is there is little mention of the role of the Sire in tutoring the Childe. Most embraces aren't impulsive bite and run affairs; in most cases the Sire has made the conscious decision to embrace their Childe for a reason, and would do their best to not lose it to ignorance. If you want to be callous, their Childe is an investment and it is in their interest to protect that investment, especially when the actions of the fledgling can backfire on them.<br /> <br /> I can vividly remember the IC prep sessions I had with the player of my Sire before my first LARP evening in the Elysium. I knew nothing of the WOD, and was about to be introduced as a Neonate of Clan Malkavian into a medium sized Cam Domain. So by the end of a few hours I knew about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> - the Traditions<br /> - Cam Clans, their Modus Operandi, their Disciplines. Basically what you get from the overview pages in the Core rule book, but of course biased.<br /> - Sects, and why the Cam is good and Sabbat bad. Indies were just mentioned as a side note.<br /> - Offices of the Cam and what they do<br /> - Etiquette towards said offices and elders. General etiquette around vamps: why you don't look them directly in the eyes and such.<br /> - the Traditions, again<br /> - Essentials about vitae; generations, blood bonds, ghouling, Embraces. Diablerie was <i>not</i> mentioned.<br /> - Current political standings in the Domain<br /> - Elysium, hunting grounds, local stuff<br /> - A lot of what NOT to do with specific Clans or people or in general<br /> - the seventh Tradition: Don't get caught.<br /> <br /> Granted, the character of my Sire was rather Cam-conservative, but that's about the baseline I expect Neonates to know, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:46:58-07:00","id":1516427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516423#post1516423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to see the different rationales, there are good points for whether more or less knowledge is sensible. One thing I notice is there is little mention of the role of the Sire in tutoring the Childe. Most embraces aren't impulsive bite and run affairs; in most cases the Sire has made the conscious decision to embrace their Childe for a reason, and would do their best to not lose it to ignorance. If you want to be callous, their Childe is an investment and it is in their interest to protect that investment, especially when the actions of the fledgling can backfire on them.<br /> <br /> I can vividly remember the IC prep sessions I had with the player of my Sire before my first LARP evening in the Elysium. I knew nothing of the WOD, and was about to be introduced as a Neonate of Clan Malkavian into a medium sized Cam Domain. So by the end of a few hours I knew about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> - the Traditions<br /> - Cam Clans, their Modus Operandi, their Disciplines. Basically what you get from the overview pages in the Core rule book, but of course biased.<br /> - Sects, and why the Cam is good and Sabbat bad. Indies were just mentioned as a side note.<br /> - Offices of the Cam and what they do<br /> - Etiquette towards said offices and elders. General etiquette around vamps: why you don't look them directly in the eyes and such.<br /> - the Traditions, again<br /> - Essentials about vitae; generations, blood bonds, ghouling, Embraces. Diablerie was <i>not</i> mentioned.<br /> - Current political standings in the Domain<br /> - Elysium, hunting grounds, local stuff<br /> - A lot of what NOT to do with specific Clans or people or in general<br /> - the seventh Tradition: Don't get caught.<br /> <br /> Granted, the character of my Sire was rather Cam-conservative, but that's about the baseline I expect Neonates to know, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah,<br /> <br /> I feel like the Mentor background is really underdone. So few player characters take it, even though it is incredibly useful. I suppose my rationale is that preserving the Mystery and sense of uncertainty about the setting is an end in itself. The players may know a lot more of it but the sense of dread their characters experience can be experienced vicariously. I also think the Joker's words in THE DARK KNIGHT apply.<br /> <br /> \u200b<img width=\"1024\" height=\"490\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1024/1*1LflVh8FJaO-jLtj3DtFSw.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1024/1*1LflVh8FJaO-jLtj3DtFSw.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1024/1*1LflVh8FJaO-jLtj3DtFSw.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> The big advantage of keeping your knowledge to yourself is that it can be bargained for in the Rat Race of Kindred society. It doesn't have to be a BIG boon but virtually every little bit of information can be bargained for in a way that can be useful in the long term. It's a minor favor, potentially, to say, &quot;Could you tell me about the Thirteen Clans&quot; or &quot;What, exactly, is a fucking Hecata and why are eveyrone acting like they're Sauron meets the Godfather?&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of us really enjoy talking in-character about lore and having your character comment on everything everyone already knows OOC is a cheap session but a session it is.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, the Salubri are what now, exactly?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Vegetarian humane healer vampires.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Bullshit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:52:38-07:00","id":1516428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516419#post1516419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, your game, so no one in the position to argue with you, I just would like to add, in my opinion the Camarilla Clans, as much as they are famous of denying the Antediluvian's existence, are strangely enough, - or not that strangely - are not different than then sabbat about them regarding existence<br /> Venture - no question tehere, they are expected to know their line back to Caine<br /> Toreador - they are either proud of Arikel alegedly the oldest Antediluvian and rub it under the nose of the Ventrue to piss of the &quot;Firstborns&quot; and familiar with the tale of the love between Absimilaird and Arikel, or don't really care.<br /> Malkavian - Okay, they are wyldcards, but considering the Madness Network and the constant whispering, voices of others or dead, alive yet to be Embraced Malkavians...? But okay, thay are the one that probably know nothing - yet spontaneusly burst of ancient tales and knowledge then blinking, what just happened?<br /> Nosferatu - their whole deal and Clan is centered around Absimiliard and the Nictuku tries to hunt them down... and the little stunt Baba Yaga pulled left a lasting impression on the world<br /> Brujah - no matter its age, I think you can't find a Brujah who don't know about Carthage and not blame the Venture for its fall...<br /> Tremere - as you said, know<br /> Gangrel - now this is a tricky one. Embraced and left alone to prove themselves... BUT after they managed to survive? The vital part of a Gangrel Gathering to tell stories and remember lineages up to Ennoia herself<br /> Lasombra - yep, they know and proud of it, either because they killed it, or either becasue they were better than their ancient and survived<br /> Tzimsice - See Lasombra<br /> Cappadocian/Hekata - yeah... you won't find one who don't know papa Cappadocius (or if you are a giovanni uncle Augie)<br /> Salubri - same as Cappadocian<br /> Ravnos - If the Week of Nightamre happened... ouch. If not, really depends of the region, the eastern Ravons are different than the western Ravnos who probably don&quot;t even know the Eastern Ravnos exist<br /> Followers of Set/Minisitry - another clan centered around their God, even the Ministry branch tho' becasue of the natrue of the Clan, varibaly degree of Truth<br /> Banu Haqim - Same as above with an added Ur-Shulgi\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting case and one that people can certainly argue. The question of things like Generation and it's role in Camarilla society certainly suggests that at least some of them take the concept seriously and even if you don't believe in Caine, a lot of people certainly do believe in the concept of a founder and that the &quot;purity of your blood&quot; is a social cue in your favor.<br /> <br /> Damien may just be a Neonate but he was a 6th generation Neonate and that meant he was either a potential source of vast power if you can diablerize him (sadly, he's trained himself as a wrecking ball) or a potential ally.<br /> <br /> I do think the Antediluvians are something that ELDERS tend to discuss at Elysium more than Neonates at the Succubus Club. It's a kind of thing where you go up to someone, they talk in a whisper to come back to their place, and they show you their copy of the Book of Nod or tell you a SCARRRYY story that they heard from their sire that is still worth a major boon.<br /> <br /> It's not that I think the answers aren't available, it's just a think it's better to make the players want to seek them in-game.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T03:53:41-07:00","id":1516429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516275#post1516275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess just the basic, something like that:<br /> <br /> Brujah: Anarchs, idealistic and impulsive, prone to anger, cannon fodder in most cases, but have some unity among themselves and some of them are capable leaders, but this is very rare. Use them, but beware of them.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Similar to Brujah but without the idealistic part, wild as animals and don't feel good in cities, but aren't necessarily dumb, if you see one of them that looks more animal than human then stay away from him.<br /> <br /> Toreador: Pretty face, snub nose, dresses well, thinks they knows more than they actually does, some say they can still fuck, are good with gossip, but don't trust them.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Monsters that live in the sewers, they know a lot of things even what you think they don't know, they usually open their mouths when they receive the right payment along with some praise, but they can still screw you by giving you the wrong information, don't provoke them and avoid them if you can.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: Same as the toreador, but with more money and more bosses, as dangerous as their money.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Mages and usurpers, that says all you need to know and why you shouldn't trust them, associating with them has its advantages, but be aware of the risks. (Script tool)<br /> <br /> Malkavian: Unpredictable freaks and bores until proven otherwise, which usually isn't the case, avoid destroying them, even if it's very tempting.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Think of a Ventrue who dresses like a Toreador and uses shadows.<br /> <br /> Tzimice: ???<br /> <br /> Ravnos: Arms merchants and mercenaries, do not trust them under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> Ministry: Treacherous snakes, if you can, rip off the head and don't listen to anything they tell you.<br /> <br /> Giovanni: Mafiosi and dangerous, don't underestimate them and remember where there is one there must be more. Try not to provoke them and don't even go near their relatives.<br /> <br /> Saulot: Two options: Avoid them, they always bring problems; What is a Saulot?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting case and one that people can certainly argue. The question of things like Generation and it's role in Camarilla society certainly suggests that at least some of them take the concept seriously and even if you don't believe in Caine, a lot of people certainly do believe in the concept of a founder and that the &quot;purity of your blood&quot; is a social cue in your favor.<br /> Damien may just be a Neonate but he was a 6th generation Neonate and that meant he was either a potential source of vast power if you can diablerize him (sadly, he's trained himself as a wrecking ball) or a potential ally.<br /> <br /> I do think the Antediluvians are something that ELDERS tend to discuss at Elysium more than Neonates at the Succubus Club. It's a kind of thing where you go up to someone, they talk in a whisper to come back to their place, and they show you their copy of the Book of Nod or tell you a SCARRRYY story that they heard from their sire that is still worth a major boon.<br /> It's not that I think the answers aren't available, it's just a think it's better to make the players want to seek them in-game.\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T04:51:21-07:00","id":1516434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516427#post1516427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose my rationale is that preserving the Mystery and sense of uncertainty about the setting is an end in itself. The players may know a lot more of it but the sense of dread their characters experience can be experienced vicariously.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> \u200b<br /> The big advantage of keeping your knowledge to yourself is that it can be bargained for in the Rat Race of Kindred society. It doesn't have to be a BIG boon but virtually every little bit of information can be bargained for in a way that can be useful in the long term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on board with that. The first time you see what happens to someone who pissed off the Tremere Regent should be sobering. Maybe you have heard that they are WIZARDS(!) and you shouldn't give them your blood under any circumstance, but watching it go down live is something else.<br /> <br /> I think from an ST perspective, I set the line at knowledge that would prevent having a PC make a blunder out of ignorance when it would feel like a cheap Gotcha! moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T04:53:54-07:00","id":1516435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516422#post1516422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secrets are power among vampires and the majority of undead actually prefer to bargain for their information. As such, it's hard to know what's going on in another city let alone in ancient annals of Kindred history.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's secrets and then there's -stuff you should definitely know as my childer in order not to embarrass me, like who the Lasombra are- Bargaining for every tidbit of what should be every day knowledge is just petty. <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course there's some knowledge you shouldn't share with fledglings<br /> Diablerie? Never heard of it. <br /> Gehenna? Some quackery. <br /> Golconda? I got a bridge to sell ya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:35:54-07:00","id":1516451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516435#post1516435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's secrets and then there's -stuff you should definitely know as my childer in order not to embarrass me, like who the Lasombra are- Bargaining for every tidbit of what should be every day knowledge is just petty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course there's some knowledge you shouldn't share with fledglings<br /> Diablerie? Never heard of it.<br /> Gehenna? Some quackery.<br /> Golconda? I got a bridge to sell ya.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the second two could easily be proliferated among Kindred by bad faith actors as well. In Bloodlines, there's a scene where you can tell a Thin Blood that he can become a human again by killing the head vampire or drinking unicorn's blood.<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you never heard of Golconda? It's the only salvation among our kind! I can teach you the secrets of it if you pledge for me ten years of service! Oh and you have to drink my blood three times to create the sacred bond.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wonder how common the Blood Bond is known of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T07:12:37-07:00","id":1516454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516427#post1516427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The big advantage of keeping your knowledge to yourself is that it can be bargained for in the Rat Race of Kindred society. It doesn't have to be a BIG boon but virtually every little bit of information can be bargained for in a way that can be useful in the long term. It's a minor favor, potentially, to say, &quot;Could you tell me about the Thirteen Clans&quot; or &quot;What, exactly, is a fucking Hecata and why are eveyrone acting like they're Sauron meets the Godfather?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sharing the kind of information available with a single dot of Occult or Politics -- which is what we're discussing here -- is, at best, a minor boon if it's a time-consuming task on a night when the would-be creditor has other shit to do. And it'll likely be considered a boon owed by the sire or whomever has claimed accounting for the neonate, for not having taken the time to explain rudimentary information themselves.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's almost certainly a trivial boon. Lest we forget, it's an insult to negotiate or call in a trivial boon, and Harpies don't even track them as most vampires repay in kind of their own volition quickly and without complaint. Trivial boons are prestation in name only, and more custom than currency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T07:29:35-07:00","id":1516455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516454#post1516454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sharing the kind of information available with a single dot of Occult or Politics -- which is what we're discussing here -- is, at best, a minor boon if it's a time-consuming task on a night when the would-be creditor has other shit to do. And it'll likely be considered a boon owed by the sire or whomever has claimed accounting for the neonate, for not having taken the time to explain rudimentary information themselves.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's almost certainly a trivial boon. Lest we forget, it's an insult to negotiate or call in a trivial boon, and Harpies don't even track them as most vampires repay in kind of their own volition quickly and without complaint. Trivial boons are prestation in name only, and more custom than currency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harpies don't need to trade in this kind of information. By the time someone is an Ancilla, I expect they're the sort of people who actually have all of the information to be found in the V:TM handbook and maybe the Players Guide. There's still vast amounts of more information to know (say, the Sabbat Guide) but they have achieved enough to know what sort of World of Darkness exists. Elders, by contrast, probably tend to have a three occult or a high enough intelligence score that they can fake it. The Elders not only know the Vampire's rulebook and Companion but have also read their Clan Book.<br /> <br /> That's what I think the &quot;general&quot; idea of each level of vampire knowledge is.<br /> <br /> Which is to say general information costs a lot more when you're a Neonate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T08:19:10-07:00","id":1516459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516429#post1516429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an interesting case and one that people can certainly argue. The question of things like Generation and it's role in Camarilla society certainly suggests that at least some of them take the concept seriously and even if you don't believe in Caine, a lot of people certainly do believe in the concept of a founder and that the &quot;purity of your blood&quot; is a social cue in your favor.<br /> Damien may just be a Neonate but he was a 6th generation Neonate and that meant he was either a potential source of vast power if you can diablerize him (sadly, he's trained himself as a wrecking ball) or a potential ally.<br /> <br /> I do think the Antediluvians are something that ELDERS tend to discuss at Elysium more than Neonates at the Succubus Club. It's a kind of thing where you go up to someone, they talk in a whisper to come back to their place, and they show you their copy of the Book of Nod or tell you a SCARRRYY story that they heard from their sire that is still worth a major boon.<br /> It's not that I think the answers aren't available, it's just a think it's better to make the players want to seek them in-game.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you didn't reply to the wrong comment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:03:21-07:00","id":1516463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516459#post1516459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure you didn't reply to the wrong comment?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> We're discussing knowledge of the ANtediluvians, aren't we? Generation is the obvious 100% basic thing that connects a Neonate to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:06:20-07:00","id":1516464,"title":"","content":"What my Malkavian knows about the other clans in general.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: A clan of warriors and low key blood mages and power brokers that make the rest of Kindred society wary as they have strange ideas regarding amarath as a good thing.<br /> <br /> Brujah: A group of angry rebels that can rise quickly to power and burn out just as quickly.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Tough survivalists that can travel the world with far greater ease then the rest of the undead and have a keen understanding of the beast.<br /> <br /> Hecate: Giovanni whom decided to change there name for some reason and reached out to other necromantic bloodlines to join them.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Ruthless manipulators whom can summon shadows to aid them.<br /> <br /> Ministry: A vibrant clan that others overlook because of their worship of a long gone god and not understand how well connected they are to all facets of society where the other high clans would overlook.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Don't let the fact of being deformed and living underground fool you. They have sharp ears and hear and record all sorts of useful knowledge. If you really want to know what is happening in your domain, they will share it with you for price.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: A nearly extinct clan of outcasts that do dirty jobs that no one will else do.<br /> <br /> Torador: High society snobs in love with there own voices and beauty, but don't get caught in there games as you might not be able to get out of.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Upstart brats that think there blood magic makes them superior to the rest and overlook the fact that they are dealing with kindred whom been playing these games way longer then all of them combined.<br /> <br /> Tzmisce: A clan of flesh crafters of some sort.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: The so called lords and ladies of the undead with the power to back it up and try not to get on there bad side to much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Just correcting bad mistakes and missed words. 06-28-2023, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:16:31-07:00","id":1516469,"title":"","content":"Unless you dug really deep, neonates would probably only know the clans by their stereotypes, and its most likely limited to the clans anyone bothers to inform them about. So if you live in a Camarilla controlled town which only neighbours Camarilla towns/cities, you will probably only be informed about the Clans that have a presence in said town, and maybe a tid bit or two about allied clans that have no presence in said town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:33:36-07:00","id":1516470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516464#post1516464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What my Malkavian knows about the other clans in general.<br /> <br /> Banu Haqim: A clan of warriors and low key blood mages and power brokers that make the rest of Kindred society wary as the strange ideas regarding amarath as a good thing.<br /> <br /> Brujah: A group of angry rebels that can rise quickly to power and burn out just as quickly.<br /> <br /> Gangrel: Tough survivalists that can travel the world with far greater ease then the rest of the undead and have a keen understanding of the beast.<br /> <br /> Hecate: Giovanni whom decided to change there name for some reason and reached out to other necromantic bloodlines to join them.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: Ruthless manipulators whom can summon shadows to aid them.<br /> <br /> Ministry: A vibrant clan that others overlook because of their worship of a long gone god and not understand how well connected they are to all facets of society where the other high clans would overlook.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu: Don't let the fact of being deformed and living underground fool you. They have sharp ears and hear and record all sorts of useful knowledge. If you really want to know what is happening in your domain, they will share it with for price.<br /> <br /> Ravnos: A nearly extinct clan of outcasts that do dirty jobs that no one will else do.<br /> <br /> Torador: High society snobs in love with there own voices and beauty, but don't get caught in there games as you might not be able to get out of.<br /> <br /> Tremere: Upstart brats that think there blood magic makes them superior to the rest and overlook the fact that they are dealing with kindred whom been playing these games way longer then all of them combined.<br /> <br /> Tzmisce: A clan of flesh crafters of some sort.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: The so called lords and ladies of the undead with the power to back it up and try not to get on there bad side to much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool write-up!<br /> <br /> It's good to get these kind of limitations and stereotypes written out for your characters.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd note is that I actually sometimes think its fun to insert your character being incredibly wrong or hilariously misinformed about at least one.<br /> <br /> Ministry: Some people actually had a go at me and suggested this Clan was a bunch of worshipers of pagan deities, like vampire Wiccans. What a crock of shit. They seem perfectly normal to me.<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Right. Vampires who worship Cain the First Murderer and are a bunch of terrorist Satanists. It's a myth to keep Neonates in line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T11:31:41-07:00","id":1516500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516455#post1516455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Harpies don't need to trade in this kind of information.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying. I'm saying Harpies don't track trivial boons, because they're, you know, <i>trivial</i>. What is what the level of information we're discussing is worth. Not all information is of equal value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Which is to say general information costs a lot more when you're a Neonate. </div> </div> </div>Information also follows the law of supply and demand. If it's general knowledge, it's minimal value. You're talking about trading the vampire equivalent to pub trivia for minor boons or more -- and up-charging on shit like that is going to give the creditor a reputation for usury, and potentially harm their status as consequence. In other words, the cost of being an asshole about this, will be far greater than the benefit from not being an asshole.<br /> <br /> And like I said, a neonate <i>not</i> knowing basic information is going to reflect worse on whomever claimed Accounting for them, than it will the neonate. <i>They're</i> going to owe the boon, not the neonate, and it probably <i>will</i> be up-charged for the combination of inconvenience and to keep quiet about the poor Accounting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:31:05-07:00","id":1516510,"title":"","content":"This thread has gotten me thinking back to the clan stereotypes of each other described in the old core books (first and second edition especially) and the interesting implied world building that went on in those little blurbs. Now a lot of it wasn\u2019t really thoroughly fleshed out and fell away as time went on but I still think you\u2019ve got interesting tid bits in there.<br /> <br /> Example;<br /> <br /> \u2022Brujah on Tremere <i>\u201cOur arch rivals, none are worse than these manipulators\u201d</i><br /> I always recall this blurb in particular as it goes against what became accepted wisdom as time went on, that the true rivals were the Brujah and Ventrue. This quote however suggests that while yes, the Brujah do disdain the Ventrue as running dogs of the elders and hidebound tradition, they view the Tremere as a more significant threat - which makes sense really, given the view in early editions of the Tremere as being an (even more) unnatural conspiracy who was undoubtedly plotting to expand their control over all vampirism <br /> <br /> \u2022Gangrel on Tremere <i>\u201cThough they do not realize it, we are enemies. They follow the wrong path and will destroy us all.\u201d</i><br /> This blurb fits with the anti-Tremere sentiment above but obviously has more going on. On one level you could retroactively interpret this as referring to the animosity held by the Gangrel from the nights of the Omen Wars/Creation of the Gargoyles; although that begs the question of why the Tremere don\u2019t realize it - perhaps their elders keep that history secret. What I find more interesting is the second path, that they follow the wrong path and will destroy us all. When I first read this I thought it would have something to do with Gangrel being aligned with a naturalist spirituality which was in stark contrast from the rationalist occultism of the Tremere - and suspicion of whatever goals the Pyramid was moving towards. The Malkavian blurb on the Tremere also touched on this, reproaching the warlocks for their inability to accept the inevitability of the cycles which will consume them all.<br /> <br /> \u2022Nosferatu on Brujah <i>\u201cNice enough fellas, once you get past the crap\u201d</i><br /> Less high-stakes than the Tremere paranoia (which the Nosferatu do share) but a reflection of an interesting social tick. The general consensus of the Gangrel, Malkavians, and Nosferatu towards the Brujah tends to be positive, albeit they all acknowledge that the Brujah are too full of their own ideas at times. That creates an interesting dynamic imo. I feel like later blurbs became more disdainful of the Brujah but this suggests a somewhat different position - that among the more stereotypical low clans the Brujah are viewed as somewhat overblown but fundamentally well-intentioned and reliable. This works alongside their Presence and perhaps underlines why it was the Brujah who arose as the representatives of loyal opposition within the Camarilla and the vanguard of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> \u2022Toreador on Nosferatu / Gangrel: <i>\u201cThese loathsome beasts ought to have been expelled from the Camarilla long ago. They hate all beauty and despise us for ours.\u201d </i>/ <i>\u201cWe don\u2019t claim to understand them. Are they kindred at all?\u201d</i><br /> Given that the Toreador are presented as the primary social orchestra of kindred society, the views attributed to them here are interesting. They also express a wary respect for the Tremere, qualified admiration for the Brujah &amp; Malkavians, and a more-or-less affable acknowledgement of the Ventrue. Now it\u2019s well established that the Toreador and Nosferatu are anathema to one another, but imo it\u2019s never been fully and effectively fleshed out. We can understand the arguments the Toreador in abstract can make: that the Nosferatu are fundamentally breaches of the Masquerade (which Gangrel can also become) but furthermore we can assume they have a genuine loathing based upon their value of the aesthetics. However this is not fully fleshed out imo. Do the Toreador actually push for anti-Nosferatu policies? Do they want Nosferatu to be barred from Camarilla society (except perhaps for elders and those who can use high enough Obfuscate to be presentable) and kept to the outside? Is their opinion of the Gangrel supported by similar policy or more a recognition of the increasing likelihood of Gangrel to avoid society as they age (unimaginable to the typical Toreador)? How reflected is this in the actual governance of Princes and the Camarilla? <br /> <br /> \u2022Tremere Quote <i>\u201cWe must survive Gehenna and establish the tenets of the New World Order once the horror is overcome. If we are to succeed, we must control the other clans. No more time can be wasted. If they cannot be convinced to aid us, they must be forced.\u201d</i><br /> I feel this quote is best suited to describe the Tremere\u2019s own section than any of their views on the other hand (but for the record: they seem to view the Ventrue and Nosferatu as their most pressing threats but acknowledge that the Brujah will probably have to be addressed with conflict as well, more or less admire the Malkavians &amp; Gangrel but seem to assume they\u2019ll sit out any real power struggle, and consider the Toreador and their society to largely be an afterthought worthy of disdain). This basically lines up with the suspicions given above but it also further highlights a conflict that was largely pushed into the background until Gehenna (kind of like the Inconnu were). It\u2019s interesting to think how this might have been put into more active use. Perhaps an assumption of the core book is that in the archetypal Camarilla domain the Tremere act as effectively an armed camp which is preparing for a magickal Armageddon which not only do they plan to survive and establish the post-apocalyptic world but in order to do so they want to harness the Camarilla itself.<br /> <br /> \u2022Ventrue on Malkavians <i>\u201cThey are not half as crazy as they claim to be.\u201d</i><br /> The Venture clan burbs are interesting because they are basically affable but reserved towards most clans (Gangrel, Nosferatu, Toreador, Tremere). The only clan they have no good word for is basically the Brujah, more in keeping with later developments than the Brujah themselves are here (although to be sure they don\u2019t like the Ventrue, they simply consider them a less pressing threat than the Tremere). The reason I chose their Malkavian quote to highlight is two-fold. One it brings up another old chestnut of other vampires half-wondering if the Malkavians might not be putting them on for some unknown purpose. The other half is that I think that it interestingly highlights the paranoid neuroses of the clan which could be easily overlooked amongst their respectable demeanor and aloof bearing but which bleeds through in places (such as the Antitribu, the inevitable paranoia of Ventrue princes, and their dread of the maybe non-existent \u2018Secret Masters\u2019).<br /> <br /> The reason I bring this up is that it seems an interesting way to seed world building in the setting, through these stereotype blurbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:09:08-07:00","id":1516543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516470#post1516470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool write-up!<br /> <br /> It's good to get these kind of limitations and stereotypes written out for your characters.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd note is that I actually sometimes think its fun to insert your character being incredibly wrong or hilariously misinformed about at least one.<br /> <br /> Ministry: Some people actually had a go at me and suggested this Clan was a bunch of worshipers of pagan deities, like vampire Wiccans. What a crock of shit. They seem perfectly normal to me.<br /> <br /> Sabbat: Right. Vampires who worship Cain the First Murderer and are a bunch of terrorist Satanists. It's a myth to keep Neonates in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I was trying to figure out how much a kindred embraced in the later half of the 19th century would realistically know and loved puzzles and mysteries in general and his own personal bias could get in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:17:22-07:00","id":1516555,"title":"","content":"In terms of what characters should know about clans (assuming it is the standard neonate under 25 years as a vampire), my rule of thumb is that characters should be able to know as much as they on their own clan as is contained in the Players Guide, and as much of the other clans as described in the two page spreads for each clan in their sect. For clans outside their sect, it's probably more like a one or two paragraph synopsis. For the Sabbat, don't use the corebook for the anti-tribu descriptions, but their descriptions in the Sabbat book.<br /> <br /> Of course, if players want to know less, they can know less. If they want to know more at the beginning of the game, they'll need some kind of mechanical justification (a Merit like Clan Friendship, a Background like Mentor). Everything else they need to learn in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:34:31-07:00","id":1516559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516427#post1516427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Mentor background is really underdone. So few player characters take it, even though it is incredibly useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. In many ways, many characters should have a 1 dot Mentor representing their sire, but almost none do. I attribute it to two things. <br /> <br /> On the player's side, many players don't know how their ST is going to interpret this. It might be completely useless as an actual advantage because the ST might not give them anything more than what other players are to get anyway. Or just as a means of plot exposition, which again benefits the group as a whole not them specifically. Or they are concerned the ST will turn it into a disadvantage by making the mentor too manipulative or controlling. Of all the Backgrounds, it is the one the PC controls the least and the ST controls the most. So many players don't see a real advantage to it. It is risky compared to something like Generation where the benefits are obvious.<br /> <br /> On the ST's side, the ST may not know how to portray the Mentor relationship. They are afraid it is either going to provide the PC all the answers which undermines the point of presenting plots for the PCs to figure out themselves, or they overreact and essentially give the PC nothing other than what the PC could get just roleplaying with any other NPC. They need to figure out the sweet spot.<br /> <br /> The Mentor background really needs both the PC and ST to collaborate on what the relationship should be, and the kind of things that Mentor could provide. And why the PC is his protege or mentee.<br /> <br /> When I was running my Chicago chronicle which started in the 1920s, one player (not familiar at all with the classic CbN books) wanted to play an eighth generation Ventrue. I told him it was possible, but that he'd have to be the childe of the Prince. Did he want that? He enthusiastically said yes. I then asked him if he wanted any points in Mentor. He said no.<br /> <br /> So play begins and he discovers he's a childe of Lodin. Then he learns there are a ton of other childer of Lodin, which makes him a lot less special. Every time he goes to Lodin to get some help, he doesn't get a whole lot. It's not exactly frustrating, but it's not what he expected when I said he'd be the childe of the Prince. So at some point I take him aside and let him know that Lodin is handling a lot of things, and he expects the player to do well on his own and not be a burden. He's now released so it is time for him to prove himself to Lodin and make his investment worthwhile. When the player asked if he could get anything more, I asked him if he had any dots in Mentor (which we both knew he did not), and he just nodded. He understood my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T09:47:51-07:00","id":1516663,"title":"","content":"Onto the Sects that my Malkavian has a view point on.<br /> <br /> Anarchs: Rebel &quot;teens&quot; who are fighting against mommy &amp; daddy sire and will become just like them down the road and I'm considered a member of this sect by default rather then any ideals they spout. I have better things to do then waste time on tedious politics when I have possibly forever to learn all types of lore.<br /> <br /> Camarilla: The big club where all the so called kings and queens of the night gather in secret to plot against each other to get a slight edge on there rivals. In other words just like the Anarchs only better organized at running our society nightly affairs.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu: I'm not sure if they really exist at all and there just an excuse that our elders use when there plans go awry. My grandsire claims that they do exist or did exist at some point during the the time of Rome decline. But it's all third or fourth hand rumors with no hard facts.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat: Let's get this straight for my own amusement. We had a Sect of fearful monsters waging a war against there antiduvlian founders various so called plots and disdained humanity in general. I'm shocked that they lasted as long as it did before they wised up and learned that the beings they fought against couldn't care less or were aware about there crusade against them. or that they didn't bring hunters down upon us much sooner and they call my clan insane?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-30-2023, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T14:08:32-07:00","id":1516689,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Sects: there's the Cam, then there's the Cam, then there's the Cam. Then there's a few bloodthirsty cults. <br /> <br /> The Cam/OG 7 Clans are : <br /> Brujah- Charming fellows but prone to bullshit. physically terrifying, Prone to frenzy so don't tick them off, and don't try to exploit that fact because the whole clan will get involved. They often see everything as a challenge to overcome but aren't very good at holding the hills they take. <br /> Gangrel- Rugged survival types, usually live in areas other kindred don't want, devolve into beast-mashups when they frenzy, odd powers -insert fairly decent assessment of protean 1-5 here- <br /> <b>Malkavians</b>- They could be anyone, it's very hard to generalize because they diffuse across all walks of life and yet remain organized and resultingly well informed. They're usually pretty smart (unless they're a player character) <br /> Nosferatu- Reliable mercenaries. Their information is good unless they want you dead. Still, they're unsavory and you best keep your relations with them on the downlow while also doing your best not to offend them. <br /> Toreador- Not particularly good at anything as a clan but not bad at anything either. They're generalists, and that gives them strength but can also be something of a crutch as many are all-too capable of living in mediocrity. Toreador are the best and worst of kindred. They're not terribly unified as a clan but usually have large social networks regardless. Oh, and if you want to fuck with one, get a really fancy bauble and dangle it in front of them... <br /> Tremere- It's a business. The entire clan is a corporation. <br /> Ventrue- Charming and predictable. With a specific herd to protect, Ventrue make for amicable neighbours. The conservative nature of the Ventrue makes them reliable. With strong clan bonds, they build and maintain backing like no other clan. Very good friends to have. <br /> <br /> <br /> The others though? <br /> Assamites: Dangerous, bloodthirsty savages of a cannibal cult. Call for backup and root them out. <br /> Followers of Set: generous friends but keep some distance: don't fall for their traps and don't drink the cool-aid. <br /> Giovanni- Incestuous corpse-fuckers with a lot of money and ghostly slaves. <br /> Lasombra: Psychotic Bastards with shadow powers. <br /> Ravnos- bastards with illusions. They envy and hate high-humanity vampires because they know they can never be one with their cursed bloodline.<br /> Tzmisce- Literal cancer. <br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodlines? Depends who's relevant to your local city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T04:22:33-07:00","id":1516876,"title":"","content":"I wrote an entire article about WHAT DO VAMPIRE PCS KNOW and adjusted it to be slightly more forgiving thanks to feedback here.<br /> <br /> I hope you guys enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/07/how-much-should-vampire-pcs-know.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/07/how-much-should-vampire-pcs-know.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/07/how-much-should-vampire-pcs-know.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/07/how-much-should-vampire-pcs-know.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T00:45:14-07:00","id":1518617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1516663#post1516663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onto the Sects that my Malkavian has a view point on.<br /> <br /> Anarchs: Rebel &quot;teens&quot; who are fighting against mommy &amp; daddy sire and will become just like them down the road and I'm considered a member of this sect by default rather then any ideals they spout. I have better things to do then waste time on tedious politics when I have possibly forever to learn all types of lore.<br /> <br /> Camarilla: The big club where all the so called kings and queens of the night gather in secret to plot against each other to get a slight edge on there rivals. In other words just like the Anarchs only better organized at running our society nightly affairs.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu: I'm not sure if they really exist at all and there just an excuse that our elders use when there plans go awry. My grandsire claims that they do exist or did exist at some point during the the time of Rome decline. But it's all third or fourth hand rumors with no hard facts.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat: Let's get this straight for my own amusement. We had a Sect of fearful monsters waging a war against there antiduvlian founders various so called plots and disdained humanity in general. I'm shocked that they lasted as long as it did before they wised up and learned that the beings they fought against couldn't care less or were aware about there crusade against them. or that they didn't bring hunters down upon us much sooner and they call my clan insane?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your character has any knowledge, notion, idea, or confirmations in regard to the Tal'Mahe'Ra ? Certainly most Kindred would find useful to have at least some decent information and knowledge in regard to this Sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T03:16:34-07:00","id":1518624,"title":"","content":"Few, if anyone, should know the Tal'Mahe'Ra exist.<br /> <br /> Even many of its agents in the Skinlands are ignorant of who they really serve, much less the scope of their operations or intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T05:54:02-07:00","id":1518635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516202-what-do-vampires-know-of-other-clans-in-your-games?p=1518624#post1518624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few, if anyone, should know the Tal'Mahe'Ra exist.<br /> <br /> Even many of its agents in the Skinlands are ignorant of who they really serve, much less the scope of their operations or intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a fair point. I do recall this elite and mysterious themes and atmiosphere from reading the Tal'Mahe'Ra V20 book.<br /> <br /> Though on the other hand a dedicated and honest effort could very well discover or lead to some clear information about this Sect. Just as there are experts in hiding, casting shadows, and creating conspiraces and puzzles, so there are also specialists who can break through them or resolve seemingly difficult situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}